{
  "name": "hawkmoth",
  "_about": "A hawkmoth -- the elephant hawk-moth (Deilephila elpenor), 4 cm long and 6.5 cm across the wings: a fat spindle body, olive green striped rosy pink; long narrow olive forewings swept back flat into a delta, banded and edged pink; the hindwings pink with a black base peeping out behind them; a thick head with big eyes, pale thread antennae thickening toward a hooked tip. Coat: the small elephant hawk-moth (D. porcellus, more pink). Written whole by tools/creaturegen/rework/winged/butterflies.py on insectlib.py + wlib.py (each wing one sheet, its upperside's painting laid on it as thin sheets in layers -- the 2D butterflies' own paintings, assets/butterflies/; the wings beat in the variant \"flying\").",
